onboarding.intro.title	Welcome to BettrFG
onboarding.intro.body	This tour covers the tabs and the side wheel. It takes about a minute.
onboarding.btn.skip	Skip
onboarding.btn.lets_go	Start
onboarding.btn.next	Next
onboarding.btn.finish	Finish
onboarding.tabsintro.title	Tabs
onboarding.tabsintro.body	BettrFG is built from one or more tabs. Each tab holds the settings for the one thing it covers, such as your bean, the nametags or Creative.
onboarding.tabs.title	Opening a tab
onboarding.tabs.body	Click the highlighted tab title to open it.
onboarding.switch.title	Changing a tab
onboarding.switch.body	Right-click the same title to list the other tabs.
onboarding.picktab.title	Tab list
onboarding.picktab.body	Any slot can hold any tab. Select one from the list.
onboarding.closetab.title	Closing a tab
onboarding.closetab.body	Click the title again to close it.
onboarding.toggleui.title	Showing the tabs
onboarding.toggleui.body	The tabs are hidden right now. Press {0} to show them, and the same keys hide them again.
onboarding.wheel.title	Side wheel
onboarding.wheel.body	Press {0} to open the side wheel. Settings windows open from here.
onboarding.tweaks.title	Tweaks
onboarding.tweaks.body	Select the Tweaks icon on the wheel.
onboarding.tweaksopen.title	Tweaks
onboarding.tweaksopen.body	Each row here turns one BettrFG change to the game on or off.
onboarding.tweaksclose.title	Closing a window
onboarding.tweaksclose.body	Select the same icon again to close the window.
help.btn.yes	Show me
help.btn.no	No thanks
help.btn.next	Next
help.btn.done	Close
help.profiles.title	Profiles
help.profiles.ask	Show a short guide to Profiles?
help.profiles.p1	A profile is a saved customization tagged with a player name. When that player appears in a round, their bean uses that look on your screen.
help.profiles.p2	Export saves your current look to a .bfgprofile file, tagged with your own name. Send it to another player so they see you that way.
help.profiles.p3	Import loads a .bfgprofile file. You can also drop the file onto the bar. Imported profiles appear in the list below with ON and DEL buttons.
help.profiles.p4	Profiles are local. They change what you see, not what other players see.
help.menumusic.title	Menu Music
help.menumusic.ask	Show a short guide to Menu Music?
help.menumusic.p1	Menu Music replaces the song that plays behind the Fall Guys menus.
help.menumusic.p2	This switch turns it on and off. When off, the game's own menu music plays.
help.menumusic.p3	Refresh reloads the track list from the BettrFG catalogue.
help.menumusic.p4	GET downloads a track. USE sets it as your menu song. Downloaded tracks are cached and only download once.
help.uitab.title	User Interface
help.uitab.ask	Show a short guide to the User Interface tab?
help.uitab.p1	This tab has four sections: Foreground, Font, Background and Scaling.
help.uitab.p2	Foreground recolours the screens shown during a show, such as Qualified and Winner. The arrows select which screen to preview.
help.uitab.p3	Edit opens the colour settings for the selected screen.
help.uitab.p4	Font replaces the game's typeface. Fonts added here apply to every menu.
help.uitab.p5	Background changes the Fall Guys menu screen backgrounds. Each screen can use a gradient or a pattern.
help.uitab.p6	Scaling sets the Fall Guys UI scale and how close it sits to the screen edges.
help.uitab.p7	Use this bar to move between the four sections.
onboarding.done.title	Tour complete
onboarding.done.body	Tabs hold the features. The side wheel holds the settings windows.
